Use int64_t to calculate paste box dimensions (CVE-2026-59199)

The paste box dimensions xsize/ysize were computed as (dx1 - dx0) using
32-bit int arithmetic. Crafted coordinates near INT_MIN/INT_MAX cause the
subtraction to overflow, producing a bogus (large/negative) size that
bypasses the subsequent dimension-mismatch check and leads to
out-of-bounds access. Compute the differences in int64_t so the values
are represented faithfully and the mismatch check rejects them.

Upstream fix: ceefc348eb3c3844c7f9796ef2cc3a7dd5fbba7b

