Calculate JPEG2000 total_component_width for each tile in isolation

CVE-2026-59204 (CWE-770): the JPEG2000 decoder accumulated
total_component_width across all tiles instead of resetting it per tile.
A crafted multi-tile J2K file could carry the running sum forward, causing
the per-tile tile_bytes overflow guard to be computed against an inflated
width and permitting an under-sized allocation / out-of-bounds access.

Backport of upstream commit 13ada41172142f2fd9f0906f615a00ea623a11ca
(python-pillow/Pillow PR #9704). Move the total_component_width declaration
and zero-initialisation inside the per-tile loop body so it is recomputed
in isolation for each tile.

