Add decompression bomb checks to FontFile classes (CVE-2026-55379)

Pillow before 12.3.0 called Image.new() from BDF/PCF/FontFile glyph paths
using attacker-controlled dimensions without Image._decompression_bomb_check(),
bypassing Pillow's documented pixel-limit protection and allowing excessive
memory allocation (CWE-789).

Add the missing checks before glyph and atlas allocations.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/0a263e6264aa5399988d9acd3bbfbca2ca3ec77d (PR #9711)

